WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:08.943
We traced account setup, one service workflow in business customer onboarding.

2
00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:13.897
Across the bank, other customer journeys have different needs.

3
00:00:14.227 --> 00:00:17.675
Business loans. Mortgages. New deposit accounts.

4
00:00:17.905 --> 00:00:21.417
Card disputes. KYC reviews. Service calls.

5
00:00:22.297 --> 00:00:25.127
If each becomes another long mapping project,

6
00:00:25.167 --> 00:00:27.911
less time is left to decide what to improve.

7
00:00:28.891 --> 00:00:32.147
RE-ViVE starts with the records the bank already keeps.

8
00:00:32.437 --> 00:00:35.821
The core. The CRM. Loan and service systems.

9
00:00:36.151 --> 00:00:39.513
Source access is read-only. Nothing is written back.

10
00:00:39.793 --> 00:00:44.905
The data is copied to an agreed environment: your servers, ours, or the cloud.

11
00:00:45.685 --> 00:00:47.704
We work out how the records link up.

12
00:00:47.924 --> 00:00:51.073
Your team helps confirm the sources and business meaning.

13
00:00:51.563 --> 00:00:55.630
Once usable sources are connected and the environment is ready,

14
00:00:55.610 --> 00:00:58.162
the initial view takes about ten business days.

15
00:00:58.442 --> 00:01:02.786
Built from operational records, and refreshed as those records update.

16
00:01:03.666 --> 00:01:06.837
Within business onboarding, add the next service workflow.

17
00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:10.152
Each has its own records, steps and readiness goals.

18
00:01:10.432 --> 00:01:12.941
Account setup. Then ACH setup.

19
00:01:13.171 --> 00:01:17.281
Wire setup. And user entitlements, so services can be used.

20
00:01:17.661 --> 00:01:20.831
Relevant records already connected can carry over.

21
00:01:21.161 --> 00:01:25.975
One onboarding process. Multiple service workflows, automatically mapped.

22
00:01:26.855 --> 00:01:30.900
When work changes, the connected records show the new execution.

23
00:01:30.970 --> 00:01:33.031
The map updates from that evidence.

24
00:01:33.911 --> 00:01:38.063
Teams can ask in plain words about the wider onboarding process.

25
00:01:38.343 --> 00:01:42.538
Use the answers to guide investigation of the underlying records.

26
00:01:43.418 --> 00:01:46.802
Before building with AI, model a change to an activity.

27
00:01:47.082 --> 00:01:49.741
See its estimated effect on end-to-end time.

28
00:01:49.961 --> 00:01:53.046
A scenario to evaluate, not a promised result.

29
00:01:54.126 --> 00:01:56.251
Start with one journey you care about.

30
00:01:56.531 --> 00:02:00.833
Your records. About ten business days once sources and setup are ready.

31
00:02:01.113 --> 00:02:02.982
Then decide where to go next.